<div class="phead"><div class="wrap"><ol class="crumbs"><li><a href="{{ PathBase }}/">Home</a></li><li>Pricing</li></ol><p class="kick">Pricing (story figures)</p><h1>Priced on events metered. Never on seats.</h1><p class="lede">Every plan includes unlimited dashboard users, every integration, and invoice explain. Pick a plan by volume; switch any month. This is a fictional product, so there is nothing to buy here.</p></div></div>
<section class="sec tight"><div class="wrap"><div class="tiers">{% for p in Target.Items %}{%- assign x=p.PublishedContent -%}{%- capture bd -%}{{ x.badge }}{%- endcapture -%}<div class="tier{% if bd != "" %} hi{% endif %}">{% if bd != "" %}<span class="bdg">{{ x.badge }}</span>{% endif %}<h3><a href="{{ PathBase }}/{{ p.RoutePath }}" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:none">{{ p.PrimaryField }}</a></h3><div class="price">{{ x.price_label }} <small>{{ x.price_unit }}</small></div><p class="muted" style="margin:0">{{ x.best_for }}</p><p style="margin:0;font:700 14px var(--mono)">{{ x.included_events }}<br><span class="muted" style="font-weight:500">{{ x.overage }}</span></p><ul>{%- assign inc = x.includes | split: "|" -%}{% for li in inc %}<li>{{ li | strip }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul><div class="use" style="margin-top:auto">{{ x.example }}</div></div>{% endfor %}</div>
<h2 style="margin:64px 0 18px">What every plan includes</h2><table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th>Included</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Dashboard users</td><td>Unlimited, on every plan. Finance, support and engineering all get a login.</td></tr><tr><td>Invoice explain</td><td>Every invoice line traces back to price, aggregate and events — in the UI and the API.</td></tr><tr><td>Late-event window</td><td>72 hours by default, configurable up to 30 days on Scale and Enterprise.</td></tr><tr><td>Data export</td><td>Raw events, aggregates and invoices to S3-compatible storage, daily.</td></tr><tr><td>Retention</td><td>Raw events 13 months; aggregates and invoices for the life of the account.</td></tr></tbody></table>
<div class="faq" style="margin-top:56px;max-width:880px"><h2 style="margin-bottom:12px">Pricing questions</h2><details open><summary>What counts as an event?</summary><p>One JSON record sent to the ingest API or read from a connected source, after deduplication. Duplicates dropped on your idempotency key are not billed.</p></details><details><summary>Why not per seat?</summary><p>Usage billing touches finance, support, sales and engineering. Charging per seat would push teams to share logins, and shared logins break the audit trail.</p></details><details><summary>What happens if we go over?</summary><p>Nothing stops. Overage is billed at the plan's published rate, and you get an alert at 80% and 100% of included usage.</p></details><details><summary>Is there a self-hosted option?</summary><p>Enterprise includes a single-tenant deployment in your own cloud account (story). The ledger schema is documented, so your data is never stuck.</p></details></div></div></section>
